# Git commits

## Commit message format

Use:

`type(scope): message.`

Rules:
- **`type`** and **`scope`** are lowercase
- **always include a scope**
- **end with a period**
- keep it short and specific (optimize for “why”)

Common `type` values:
- `feat`: user-visible feature
- `fix`: bug fix
- `docs`: docs-only changes (README, prompts, etc.)
- `test`: tests only (unit/e2e/visual)
- `refactor`: non-behavior refactor
- `style`: formatting / non-functional styling
- `chore`: maintenance (scripts, tooling)
- `build`: build system changes
- `ci`: CI config changes
- `perf`: performance improvements

Common `scope` values in this repo:
- `ui`, `content`, `post`, `i18n`, `a11y`, `testing`, `prompts`, `deps`

Examples:
- `feat(ui): add empty-locale callout on /es/.`
- `fix(i18n): translate header title and tooltips.`
- `test(e2e): cover mermaid fullscreen and close.`
- `docs(readme): add architecture and testing diagrams.`
- `chore(deps): upgrade astro from 5.16.0 to 5.16.11.`

## Commit methodology (lightweight)

- **One commit per logical change**. If it’s two independent changes, split it.
- **Run the right checks** before committing:
  - UI/content: `bun run test:e2e` (or at least the relevant spec)
  - Utilities: `bun run test:unit`
  - When in doubt: `bun run check`
- **If you fix a regression**, add/tighten a test in the same PR/series.
- Avoid committing secrets (`.env`, credentials).

